# Four-Tier Data Architecture

## Overview

Data is partitioned across 4 tiers optimized for access pattern, latency, and cost:

| Tier | Engine | Latency | Data | Cost at 1M users |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Hot** | Cloudflare D1 (SQLite at edge) | <5ms | Live sessions, schedules, rosters, presence, balances, gates | ~$5/mo |
| **Warm** | PostgreSQL | 20-50ms | Complex relational, auth, billing, JSONB profiles, FKs | ~$50/mo |
| **Cold** | R2 SQL (Apache Iceberg) | 100-500ms | Historical analytics, trends, aggregations, ML features | ~$2/mo |
| **Semantic** | Cloudflare Vectorize | 10-30ms | Memory search, wisdom lookup, vault search, annotations | ~$5/mo |

PostgreSQL is the **source of truth** for all data. D1 and R2 are read-optimized caches that sync from PG.

## Architecture

```
                    ┌─ D1 (Hot: 30s sync) ── Edge Workers
PostgreSQL ────────┤
(source of truth)  ├─ R2 Iceberg (Cold: 60s CDC) ── R2 SQL
                   │
                   └─ Vectorize (async on write) ── Workers AI
```

